{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961208-help-applying-magic-character-beans-to-cod","id":961208,"title":"Help applying Magic Character Beans to CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T13:33:54-07:00","id":961208,"title":"Help applying Magic Character Beans to CoD","content":"I'm planning on running a CoD bluebook chronicle after my group finishes its current Pathfinder campaign. Several people in my group have previously played nWoD, and a couple of us played oWoD, but this will be the first time any of us will be using the updated CoD rules. I'd like to use a few things from Mirrors, including the Magic Character Beans rules, but I'm not sure exactly how to go about doing it given how deeply Beats are integrated into the new system.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd considered is having the characters regain a point of Willpower whenever they would otherwise gain a beat, as the book recommends for NPCs. The main problem with this is that it would result in the characters regaining WP at a highly accelerated rate. This would be somewhat alleviated by ditching the Virtue/Vice system, which I was considering anyway given that my group previously tended to forget about them (and Nature/Demeanor in oWoD). I'm also going to include a few other ways to spend Willpower, such as Anticipation and Declaration, so that might also balance things a bit. And, of course, there's a limit on how many WP points a character can have, meaning the players would have to be spending WP regularly or else gain nothing from resolving a Condition or whatever.<br /> <br /> Since I haven't actually used the CoD rules yet, I don't know exactly how often characters get Beats, and therefore how feasible it would be to replace Beats with WP points. I'd love to get some input and opinions about incorporating MCBs into a CoD game, and if the things I'm considering would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:37:38-07:00","id":961212,"title":"","content":"Just give 'em the Willpower instead of the beats, it'll work fine. Willpower's supposed to be a fluid resource (both in terms of spending and recovery), and Willpower from beats won't distort the rate of recovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}